IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc8-part7-lotteries.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 206 (lotteries and games of chance), 207 (permitted lotteries),
-- 207.1 (lottery scheme on an international cruise ship), 209 (cheating at play) and 213 (sexual services: stopping or impeding traffic, communicating).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc8-part7-houses.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING). A "means" definition that ends "and includes" is read as closed (marginal reading M3).
-- The core `Party` has no "board of a fair", "charitable or religious organization" or "Lieutenant Governor in Council": the licences and their issuers enter as BOOLEAN facts.

§ `Section 206 -- Offences in relation to lotteries and games of chance`

-- src:4282 | 206 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:4283 | (a) makes, prints, advertises or publishes, or causes or procures to be made, printed, advertised or published, any proposal, scheme or plan for advancing, lending, giving, selling or in any way disposing of any property by lots, cards, tickets or any mode of chance whatever;
-- src:4284 | (b) sells, barters, exchanges or otherwise disposes of, or causes or procures, or aids or assists in, the sale, barter, exchange or other disposal of, or offers for sale, barter or exchange, any lot, card, ticket or other means or device for advancing, lending, giving, selling or otherwise disposing of any property by lots, tickets or any mode of chance whatever;
-- src:4285 | (c) knowingly sends, transmits, mails, ships, delivers or allows to be sent, transmitted, mailed, shipped or delivered, or knowingly accepts for carriage or transport or conveys any article that is used or intended for use in carrying out any device, proposal, scheme or plan for advancing, lending, giving, selling or otherwise disposing of any property by any mode of chance whatever;
-- src:4286 | (d) conducts or manages any scheme, contrivance or operation of any kind for the purpose of determining who, or the holders of what lots, tickets, numbers or chances, are the winners of any property so proposed to be advanced, lent, given, sold or disposed of;
-- src:4287 | (e) conducts, manages or is a party to any scheme, contrivance or operation of any kind by which any person, on payment of any sum of money, or the giving of any valuable security, or by obligating himself to pay any sum of money or give any valuable security, shall become entitled under the scheme, contrivance or operation to receive from the person conducting or managing the scheme, contrivance or operation, or any other person, a larger sum of money or amount of valuable security than the sum or amount paid or given, or to be paid or given, by reason of the fact that other persons have paid or given, or obligated themselves to pay or give any sum of money or valuable security under the scheme, contrivance or operation;
-- src:4288 | (f) disposes of any goods, wares or merchandise by any game of chance or any game of mixed chance and skill in which the contestant or competitor pays money or other valuable consideration;
-- src:4289 | (g) induces any person to stake or hazard any money or other valuable property or thing on the result of any dice game, three-card monte, punch board, coin table or on the operation of a wheel of fortune;
-- src:4290 | (h) for valuable consideration carries on or plays or offers to carry on or to play, or employs any person to carry on or play in a public place or a place to which the public have access, the game of three-card monte;
-- src:4291 | (i) receives bets of any kind on the outcome of a game of three-card monte; or
-- src:4292 | (j) being the owner of a place, permits any person to play the game of three-card monte therein.
@ref s 206(1) (src:4282-4292)
DECLARE `s 206(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 206(1)(a) makes, prints, advertises or publishes, or causes or procures to be made, printed, advertised or published, any proposal, scheme or plan for disposing of any property by lots, cards, tickets or any mode of chance whatever`
    `s 206(1)(b) sells, barters, exchanges or otherwise disposes of, or causes or procures, or aids or assists in, the sale, barter, exchange or other disposal of, or offers for sale, barter or exchange, any lot, card, ticket or other means or device for disposing of any property by lots, tickets or any mode of chance whatever`
    `s 206(1)(c) knowingly sends, transmits, mails, ships, delivers or allows to be sent, transmitted, mailed, shipped or delivered, or knowingly accepts for carriage or transport or conveys any article that is used or intended for use in carrying out any such device, proposal, scheme or plan`
    `s 206(1)(d) conducts or manages any scheme, contrivance or operation of any kind for the purpose of determining who, or the holders of what lots, tickets, numbers or chances, are the winners of any property so proposed to be disposed of`
    `s 206(1)(e) conducts, manages or is a party to any scheme, contrivance or operation of any kind by which any person, on payment of any sum of money, or the giving of any valuable security, shall become entitled to receive a larger sum of money or amount of valuable security than the sum or amount paid or given, by reason of the fact that other persons have paid or given`
    `s 206(1)(f) disposes of any goods, wares or merchandise by any game of chance or any game of mixed chance and skill in which the contestant or competitor pays money or other valuable consideration`
    `s 206(1)(g) induces any person to stake or hazard any money or other valuable property or thing on the result of any dice game, three-card monte, punch board, coin table or on the operation of a wheel of fortune`
    `s 206(1)(h) for valuable consideration carries on or plays or offers to carry on or to play, or employs any person to carry on or play in a public place or a place to which the public have access, the game of three-card monte`
    `s 206(1)(i) receives bets of any kind on the outcome of a game of three-card monte`
    `s 206(1)(j) being the owner of a place, permits any person to play the game of three-card monte therein`

@ref s 206(1) (src:4282-4292)
GIVEN act IS A `s 206(1) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(1) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 206(1)(a) makes, prints, advertises or publishes, or causes or procures to be made, printed, advertised or published, any proposal, scheme or plan for disposing of any property by lots, cards, tickets or any mode of chance whatever` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 206(1)(b) sells, barters, exchanges or otherwise disposes of, or causes or procures, or aids or assists in, the sale, barter, exchange or other disposal of, or offers for sale, barter or exchange, any lot, card, ticket or other means or device for disposing of any property by lots, tickets or any mode of chance whatever` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 206(1)(c) knowingly sends, transmits, mails, ships, delivers or allows to be sent, transmitted, mailed, shipped or delivered, or knowingly accepts for carriage or transport or conveys any article that is used or intended for use in carrying out any such device, proposal, scheme or plan` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 206(1)(d) conducts or manages any scheme, contrivance or operation of any kind for the purpose of determining who, or the holders of what lots, tickets, numbers or chances, are the winners of any property so proposed to be disposed of` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 206(1)(e) conducts, manages or is a party to any scheme, contrivance or operation of any kind by which any person, on payment of any sum of money, or the giving of any valuable security, shall become entitled to receive a larger sum of money or amount of valuable security than the sum or amount paid or given, by reason of the fact that other persons have paid or given` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 206(1)(f) disposes of any goods, wares or merchandise by any game of chance or any game of mixed chance and skill in which the contestant or competitor pays money or other valuable consideration` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 206(1)(g) induces any person to stake or hazard any money or other valuable property or thing on the result of any dice game, three-card monte, punch board, coin table or on the operation of a wheel of fortune` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 206(1)(h) for valuable consideration carries on or plays or offers to carry on or to play, or employs any person to carry on or play in a public place or a place to which the public have access, the game of three-card monte` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 206(1)(i) receives bets of any kind on the outcome of a game of three-card monte` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 206(1)(j) being the owner of a place, permits any person to play the game of three-card monte therein` THEN JUST TRUE

@ref s 206(1) (src:4282-4292)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 206(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 206(1) (src:4282-4292)
`s 206(1) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 206(1) (src:4282-4292)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 206(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 206(1) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4294 | (2) In this section, three-card monte means the game commonly known as three-card monte and includes any other game that is similar to it, whether or not the game is played with cards and notwithstanding the number of cards or other things that are used for the purpose of playing.
@ref s 206(2) (src:4294-4294)
GIVEN `it is the game commonly known as three-card monte` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another game that is similar to it, whether or not it is played with cards and notwithstanding the number of cards or other things that are used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(2) three-card monte` MEANS
    IF `it is the game commonly known as three-card monte` OR `it is another game that is similar to it, whether or not it is played with cards and notwithstanding the number of cards or other things that are used`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "three-card monte means the game commonly known as three-card monte and includes any other game that is similar to it"

-- src:4298 | (3.1) For the purposes of this section, fair or exhibition means an event where agricultural or fishing products are presented or where activities relating to agriculture or fishing take place.
@ref s 206(3.1) (src:4298-4298)
GIVEN `it is an event where agricultural or fishing products are presented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an event where activities relating to agriculture or fishing take place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(3.1) fair or exhibition` MEANS
    IF `it is an event where agricultural or fishing products are presented` OR `it is an event where activities relating to agriculture or fishing take place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "fair or exhibition means an event where agricultural or fishing products are presented or where activities relating to agriculture or fishing take place"

-- src:4296 | (3) Paragraphs (1)(f) and (g), in so far as they do not relate to a dice game, three-card monte, punch board or coin table, do not apply to the board of an annual fair or exhibition, or to any operator of a concession leased by that board within its own grounds and operated during the fair or exhibition on those grounds.
@ref s 206(3) (src:4296-4296)
GIVEN act IS A `s 206(1) act`
      `it relates to a dice game, three-card monte, punch board or coin table` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the board of an annual fair or exhibition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an operator of a concession leased by that board within its own grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is operated during the fair or exhibition on those grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(3) paragraphs (1)(f) and (g) do not apply to the person` MEANS
    IF     (   act EQUALS `s 206(1)(f) disposes of any goods, wares or merchandise by any game of chance or any game of mixed chance and skill in which the contestant or competitor pays money or other valuable consideration`
            OR act EQUALS `s 206(1)(g) induces any person to stake or hazard any money or other valuable property or thing on the result of any dice game, three-card monte, punch board, coin table or on the operation of a wheel of fortune`)
       AND (NOT `it relates to a dice game, three-card monte, punch board or coin table`)
       AND (   `the person is the board of an annual fair or exhibition`
            OR (`the person is an operator of a concession leased by that board within its own grounds` AND `it is operated during the fair or exhibition on those grounds`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Paragraphs (1)(f) and (g), in so far as they do not relate to a dice game, three-card monte, punch board or coin table, do not apply to the board of an annual fair or exhibition, or to any operator of a concession"

-- src:4300 | (4) Every one who buys, takes or receives a lot, ticket or other device mentioned in subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 206(4) (src:4300-4300)
GIVEN `the person buys, takes or receives a lot, ticket or other device mentioned in subsection 206(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(4) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person buys, takes or receives a lot, ticket or other device mentioned in subsection 206(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who buys, takes or receives a lot, ticket or other device mentioned in subsection (1) is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 206(4) (src:4300-4300)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 206(4) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 206(4) (src:4300-4300)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 206(4) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4304 | (6) Subsection (5) does not affect any right or title to property acquired by any bona fide purchaser for valuable consideration without notice.
@ref s 206(6) (src:4304-4304)
GIVEN `the person acquired the right or title to the property as a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person gave valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had no notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(6) subsection 206(5) does not affect the right or title to the property` MEANS
    IF `the person acquired the right or title to the property as a bona fide purchaser` AND `the person gave valuable consideration` AND `the person had no notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (5) does not affect any right or title to property acquired by any bona fide purchaser for valuable consideration without notice"

-- src:4302 | (5) Every sale, loan, gift, barter or exchange of any property, by any lottery, ticket, card or other mode of chance depending on or to be determined by chance or lot, is void, and all property so sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged is forfeited to Her Majesty.
@ref s 206(5) (src:4302-4302)
GIVEN `the property was sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged by a lottery, ticket, card or other mode of chance depending on or to be determined by chance or lot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 206(5) does not affect the right or title, by s 206(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(5) the sale, loan, gift, barter or exchange is void` MEANS
    IF `the property was sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged by a lottery, ticket, card or other mode of chance depending on or to be determined by chance or lot`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every sale, loan, gift, barter or exchange of any property, by any lottery, ticket, card or other mode of chance ... is void"

@ref s 206(5) (src:4302-4302)
GIVEN `the property was sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged by a lottery, ticket, card or other mode of chance depending on or to be determined by chance or lot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 206(5) does not affect the right or title, by s 206(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(5) the property so sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged is forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the property was sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged by a lottery, ticket, card or other mode of chance depending on or to be determined by chance or lot` AND `subsection 206(5) does not affect the right or title, by s 206(6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (5) does not affect any right or title to property acquired by any bona fide purchaser for valuable consideration without notice"
        IF `the property was sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged by a lottery, ticket, card or other mode of chance depending on or to be determined by chance or lot`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all property so sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged is forfeited to Her Majesty"

-- src:4306 | (7) This section applies to the printing or publishing, or causing to be printed or published, of any advertisement, scheme, proposal or plan of any foreign lottery, and the sale or offer for sale of any ticket, chance or share, in any such lottery, or the advertisement for sale of such ticket, chance or share, and the conducting or managing of any such scheme, contrivance or operation for determining the winners in any such lottery.
@ref s 206(7) (src:4306-4306)
GIVEN `it is the printing or publishing, or causing to be printed or published, of an advertisement, scheme, proposal or plan of a foreign lottery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the sale or offer for sale of a ticket, chance or share in a foreign lottery, or the advertisement for sale of such a ticket, chance or share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the conducting or managing of a scheme, contrivance or operation for determining the winners in a foreign lottery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(7) section 206 applies to the thing done` MEANS
    IF     `it is the printing or publishing, or causing to be printed or published, of an advertisement, scheme, proposal or plan of a foreign lottery`
        OR `it is the sale or offer for sale of a ticket, chance or share in a foreign lottery, or the advertisement for sale of such a ticket, chance or share`
        OR `it is the conducting or managing of a scheme, contrivance or operation for determining the winners in a foreign lottery`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "This section applies to the printing or publishing ... of any foreign lottery, and the sale ... and the conducting or managing" (the text adds foreign lotteries; it does not say the section applies to nothing else)

-- src:4308 | (8) This section does not apply to
-- src:4309 | (a) the division by lot or chance of any property by joint tenants or tenants in common, or persons having joint interests in any such property; or
-- src:4310 | (b) [Repealed, 1999, c. 28, s. 156]
-- src:4311 | (c) bonds, debentures, debenture stock or other securities recallable by drawing of lots and redeemable with interest and providing for payment of premiums on redemption or otherwise.
@ref s 206(8) (src:4308-4311)
GIVEN `it is the division by lot or chance of any property by joint tenants or tenants in common, or persons having joint interests in any such property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is bonds, debentures, debenture stock or other securities recallable by drawing of lots and redeemable with interest and providing for payment of premiums on redemption or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(8) section 206 does not apply to the thing` MEANS
    IF     `it is the division by lot or chance of any property by joint tenants or tenants in common, or persons having joint interests in any such property`
        OR `it is bonds, debentures, debenture stock or other securities recallable by drawing of lots and redeemable with interest and providing for payment of premiums on redemption or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section does not apply to (a) ... or (c) ..." (the text says what the section does not apply to, not that it applies to everything else)

§ `Section 207 -- Permitted lotteries`

-- src:4314 | (a) for the government of a province, either alone or in conjunction with the government of another province, to conduct and manage a lottery scheme in that province, or in that and the other province, in accordance with any law enacted by the legislature of that province;
@ref s 207(1)(a) (src:4314-4314)
GIVEN `the person is the government of a province, alone or in conjunction with the government of another province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme in that province, or in that and the other province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so in accordance with a law enacted by the legislature of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1)(a) makes it lawful for the government of a province to conduct and manage a lottery scheme` MEANS
    IF `the person is the government of a province, alone or in conjunction with the government of another province` AND `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme in that province, or in that and the other province` AND `it does so in accordance with a law enacted by the legislature of that province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is lawful (a) for the government of a province ... to conduct and manage a lottery scheme in that province ... in accordance with any law enacted by the legislature of that province"

-- src:4315 | (b) for a charitable or religious organization, pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council thereof, to conduct and manage a lottery scheme in that province if the proceeds from the lottery scheme are used for a charitable or religious object or purpose;
@ref s 207(1)(b) (src:4315-4315)
GIVEN `the person is a charitable or religious organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it acts pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme in that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeds from the lottery scheme are used for a charitable or religious object or purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1)(b) makes it lawful for a charitable or religious organization to conduct and manage a lottery scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a charitable or religious organization` AND `it acts pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` AND `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme in that province` AND (NOT `the proceeds from the lottery scheme are used for a charitable or religious object or purpose`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the proceeds from the lottery scheme are used for a charitable or religious object or purpose" (marginal reading M2)
        IF `the person is a charitable or religious organization` AND `it acts pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` AND `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme in that province` AND `the proceeds from the lottery scheme are used for a charitable or religious object or purpose`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is lawful ... for a charitable or religious organization, pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council"

-- src:4316 | (c) for the board of a fair or of an exhibition, or an operator of a concession leased by that board, to conduct and manage a lottery scheme in a province where the Lieutenant Governor in Council of the province or such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council thereof has
-- src:4317 | (i) designated that fair or exhibition as a fair or exhibition where a lottery scheme may be conducted and managed, and
-- src:4318 | (ii) issued a licence for the conduct and management of a lottery scheme to that board or operator;
@ref s 207(1)(c) (src:4316-4318)
GIVEN `the person is the board of a fair or of an exhibition, or an operator of a concession leased by that board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Lieutenant Governor in Council of the province or such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council has designated that fair or exhibition as one where a lottery scheme may be conducted and managed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that authority has issued a licence for the conduct and management of a lottery scheme to that board or operator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1)(c) makes it lawful for the board of a fair or of an exhibition to conduct and manage a lottery scheme` MEANS
    IF     `the person is the board of a fair or of an exhibition, or an operator of a concession leased by that board`
       AND `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme in a province`
       AND `the Lieutenant Governor in Council of the province or such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council has designated that fair or exhibition as one where a lottery scheme may be conducted and managed`
       AND `that authority has issued a licence for the conduct and management of a lottery scheme to that board or operator`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is lawful ... for the board of a fair or of an exhibition ... to conduct and manage a lottery scheme in a province where the Lieutenant Governor in Council ... has (i) designated ... and (ii) issued a licence"

-- src:4319 | (d) for any person, pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council thereof, to conduct and manage a lottery scheme at a public place of amusement in that province if
-- src:4320 | (i) the amount or value of each prize awarded does not exceed five hundred dollars, and
-- src:4321 | (ii) the money or other valuable consideration paid to secure a chance to win a prize does not exceed two dollars;
@ref s 207(1)(d) (src:4319-4321)
GIVEN `the person acts pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme at a public place of amusement in that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount or value of each prize awarded, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the money or other valuable consideration paid to secure a chance to win a prize, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1)(d) makes it lawful for any person to conduct and manage a lottery scheme at a public place of amusement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person acts pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` AND `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme at a public place of amusement in that province`
           AND (`the amount or value of each prize awarded, in dollars` GREATER THAN 500 OR `the money or other valuable consideration paid to secure a chance to win a prize, in dollars` GREATER THAN 2)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (i) the amount or value of each prize awarded does not exceed five hundred dollars, and (ii) the money or other valuable consideration paid to secure a chance to win a prize does not exceed two dollars" (marginal reading M2)
        IF `the person acts pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` AND `it conducts and manages a lottery scheme at a public place of amusement in that province`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is lawful ... for any person, pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province ... to conduct and manage a lottery scheme at a public place of amusement in that province"

-- src:4322 | (e) for the government of a province to agree with the government of another province that lots, cards or tickets in relation to a lottery scheme that is by any of paragraphs (a) to (d) authorized to be conducted and managed in that other province may be sold in the province;
@ref s 207(1)(e) (src:4322-4322)
GIVEN `the person is the government of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it agrees with the government of another province that lots, cards or tickets in relation to a lottery scheme may be sold in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lottery scheme is by any of paragraphs (a) to (d) authorized to be conducted and managed in that other province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1)(e) makes it lawful for the government of a province to agree that lots, cards or tickets may be sold in the province` MEANS
    IF `the person is the government of a province` AND `it agrees with the government of another province that lots, cards or tickets in relation to a lottery scheme may be sold in the province` AND `the lottery scheme is by any of paragraphs (a) to (d) authorized to be conducted and managed in that other province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is lawful ... for the government of a province to agree with the government of another province that lots, cards or tickets ... may be sold in the province"

-- src:4323 | (f) for any person, pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or such other person or authority in the province as may be designated by the Lieutenant Governor in Council thereof, to conduct and manage in the province a lottery scheme that is authorized to be conducted and managed in one or more other provinces where the authority by which the lottery scheme was first authorized to be conducted and managed consents thereto;
@ref s 207(1)(f) (src:4323-4323)
GIVEN `the person acts pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or such other person or authority in the province as may be designated by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it conducts and manages in the province a lottery scheme that is authorized to be conducted and managed in one or more other provinces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority by which the lottery scheme was first authorized to be conducted and managed consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1)(f) makes it lawful for any person to conduct and manage in the province a lottery scheme authorized in another province` MEANS
    IF `the person acts pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or such other person or authority in the province as may be designated by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` AND `it conducts and manages in the province a lottery scheme that is authorized to be conducted and managed in one or more other provinces` AND `the authority by which the lottery scheme was first authorized to be conducted and managed consents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is lawful ... for any person, pursuant to a licence ... to conduct and manage in the province a lottery scheme that is authorized ... in one or more other provinces where the authority by which the lottery scheme was first authorized ... consents thereto"

-- src:4324 | (g) for any person, for the purpose of a lottery scheme that is lawful in a province under any of paragraphs (a) to (f), to do anything in the province, in accordance with the applicable law or licence, that is required for the conduct, management or operation of the lottery scheme or for the person to participate in the scheme; and
@ref s 207(1)(g) (src:4324-4324)
GIVEN `the lottery scheme is lawful in a province under any of paragraphs (a) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does the thing in the province, in accordance with the applicable law or licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is required for the conduct, management or operation of the lottery scheme or for the person to participate in the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1)(g) makes it lawful for any person to do anything required for a lottery scheme that is lawful in the province` MEANS
    IF `the lottery scheme is lawful in a province under any of paragraphs (a) to (f)` AND `the person does the thing in the province, in accordance with the applicable law or licence` AND `the thing is required for the conduct, management or operation of the lottery scheme or for the person to participate in the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is lawful ... for any person, for the purpose of a lottery scheme that is lawful in a province under any of paragraphs (a) to (f), to do anything in the province, in accordance with the applicable law or licence"

-- src:4325 | (h) for any person to make or print anywhere in Canada or to cause to be made or printed anywhere in Canada anything relating to gaming and betting that is to be used in a place where it is or would, if certain conditions provided by law are met, be lawful to use such a thing, or to send, transmit, mail, ship, deliver or allow to be sent, transmitted, mailed, shipped or delivered or to accept for carriage or transport or convey any such thing where the destination thereof is such a place.
@ref s 207(1)(h) (src:4325-4325)
GIVEN `the person makes or prints anywhere in Canada, or causes to be made or printed, anything relating to gaming and betting, or sends, transmits, mails, ships, delivers or allows it to be sent, or accepts it for carriage or transport or conveys it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be used in, or its destination is, a place where it is lawful, or would be lawful if certain conditions provided by law were met, to use such a thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1)(h) makes it lawful for any person to make or print, or send, anything relating to gaming and betting to a place where it is lawful to use it` MEANS
    IF `the person makes or prints anywhere in Canada, or causes to be made or printed, anything relating to gaming and betting, or sends, transmits, mails, ships, delivers or allows it to be sent, or accepts it for carriage or transport or conveys it` AND `it is to be used in, or its destination is, a place where it is lawful, or would be lawful if certain conditions provided by law were met, to use such a thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is lawful ... for any person to make or print anywhere in Canada ... anything relating to gaming and betting that is to be used in a place where it is or would ... be lawful to use such a thing"

-- src:4313 | 207 (1) Notwithstanding any of the provisions of this Part relating to gaming and betting, it is lawful
@ref s 207(1) (src:4313-4313)
GIVEN `the answers of paragraphs (a) to (h), by s 207(1)(a) to (h)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1) makes it lawful, notwithstanding the provisions of this Part relating to gaming and betting` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN answer YIELD answer EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers of paragraphs (a) to (h), by s 207(1)(a) to (h)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "it is lawful (a) ... (h)" (the text says what is lawful, not that nothing else is)

-- src:4327 | (2) Subject to this Act, a licence issued by or under the authority of the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province as described in paragraph (1)(b), (c), (d) or (f) may contain such terms and conditions relating to the conduct, management and operation of or participation in the lottery scheme to which the licence relates as the Lieutenant Governor in Council of that province, the person or authority in the province designated by the Lieutenant Governor in Council thereof or any law enacted by the legislature of that province may prescribe.
@ref s 207(2) (src:4327-4327)
GIVEN `the licence is one issued as described in paragraph 207(1)(b), (c), (d) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term or condition relates to the conduct, management and operation of or participation in the lottery scheme to which the licence relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of the province, the person or authority designated by the Lieutenant Governor in Council, or a law enacted by the legislature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(2) the licence may contain the term or condition` MEANS
    IF `the licence is one issued as described in paragraph 207(1)(b), (c), (d) or (f)` AND `the term or condition relates to the conduct, management and operation of or participation in the lottery scheme to which the licence relates` AND `it is prescribed by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of the province, the person or authority designated by the Lieutenant Governor in Council, or a law enacted by the legislature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this Act, a licence ... may contain such terms and conditions relating to the conduct, management and operation of or participation in the lottery scheme ... as the Lieutenant Governor in Council ... may prescribe"

-- src:4329 | (3) Every one who, for the purposes of a lottery scheme, does anything that is not authorized by or pursuant to a provision of this section
-- src:4330 | (a) in the case of the conduct, management or operation of that lottery scheme,
-- src:4331 | (i) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or
-- src:4332 | (ii) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction; or
-- src:4333 | (b) in the case of participating in that lottery scheme, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 207(3) (src:4329-4333)
DECLARE `s 207(3) role` IS ONE OF
    `s 207(3)(a) the person conducts, manages or operates the lottery scheme`
    `s 207(3)(b) the person participates in the lottery scheme`

@ref s 207(3) (src:4329-4333)
GIVEN `the thing is done for the purposes of a lottery scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is authorized by or pursuant to a provision of section 207` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(3) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the thing is done for the purposes of a lottery scheme` AND (NOT `it is authorized by or pursuant to a provision of section 207`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who, for the purposes of a lottery scheme, does anything that is not authorized by or pursuant to a provision of this section" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 207(3) (src:4329-4333)
GIVEN role IS A `s 207(3) role`
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 207(3) the class of the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER role
    WHEN `s 207(3)(a) the person conducts, manages or operates the lottery scheme` THEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
    WHEN `s 207(3)(b) the person participates in the lottery scheme` THEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 207(3)(a)(i) (src:4331-4331)
`s 207(3)(a)(i) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 207(3) (src:4329-4333)
GIVEN role IS A `s 207(3) role`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 207(3) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER role
    WHEN `s 207(3)(a) the person conducts, manages or operates the lottery scheme` THEN LIST `s 207(3)(a)(i) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
    WHEN `s 207(3)(b) the person participates in the lottery scheme` THEN LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4335 | (4) In this section, lottery scheme means a game or any proposal, scheme, plan, means, device, contrivance or operation described in any of paragraphs 206(1)(a) to (g), whether or not it involves betting, pool selling or a pool system of betting other than
-- src:4336 | (a) three-card monte, punch board or coin table;
-- src:4337 | (b) bookmaking, pool selling or the making or recording of bets, including bets made through the agency of a pool or pari-mutuel system, on any horse-race; or
-- src:4338 | (c) for the purposes of paragraphs (1)(b) to (f), a game or proposal, scheme, plan, means, device, contrivance or operation described in any of paragraphs 206(1)(a) to (g) that is operated on or through a computer, video device, slot machine or a dice game.
@ref s 207(4) (src:4335-4338)
-- Fork F4: "(other than X)" and "does not include X" are read as closing the definition: a case that is described but is one of the excluded cases is NOT a lottery scheme (JUST FALSE).
-- The other reading answers NOTHING for the excluded cases.
-- The text cites "paragraph 4(c)" in subsection (4.01) where "paragraph (4)(c)" is meant (finding F-3 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `it is a game or any proposal, scheme, plan, means, device, contrivance or operation described in any of paragraphs 206(1)(a) to (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is three-card monte, punch board or coin table` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is bookmaking, pool selling or the making or recording of bets, including bets made through the agency of a pool or pari-mutuel system, on any horse-race` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is one of paragraphs (1)(b) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is operated on or through a computer, video device, slot machine or a dice game` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(4) lottery scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is three-card monte, punch board or coin table` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than (a) three-card monte, punch board or coin table"
        IF `it is bookmaking, pool selling or the making or recording of bets, including bets made through the agency of a pool or pari-mutuel system, on any horse-race` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than ... (b) bookmaking, pool selling or the making or recording of bets"
        IF `the purpose is one of paragraphs (1)(b) to (f)` AND `it is operated on or through a computer, video device, slot machine or a dice game` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than ... (c) for the purposes of paragraphs (1)(b) to (f), a game or ... operated on or through a computer, video device, slot machine or a dice game"
        IF `it is a game or any proposal, scheme, plan, means, device, contrivance or operation described in any of paragraphs 206(1)(a) to (g)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "lottery scheme means a game or any proposal, scheme, plan, means, device, contrivance or operation described in any of paragraphs 206(1)(a) to (g)"

-- src:4340 | (4.01) In paragraph 4(c), slot machine means any automatic machine or slot machine, other than any automatic machine or slot machine that dispenses as prizes only one or more free games on that machine, that
-- src:4341 | (a) is used or intended to be used for any purpose other than selling merchandise or services; or
-- src:4342 | (b) is used or intended to be used for the purpose of selling merchandise or services if
-- src:4343 | (i) the result of one of any number of operations of the machine is a matter of chance or uncertainty to the operator,
-- src:4344 | (ii) as a result of a given number of successive operations by the operator, the machine produces different results, or
-- src:4345 | (iii) on any operation of the machine, it discharges or emits a slug or token.
@ref s 207(4.01) (src:4340-4345)
GIVEN `it is an automatic machine or slot machine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it dispenses as prizes only one or more free games on that machine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used or intended to be used for any purpose other than selling merchandise or services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used or intended to be used for the purpose of selling merchandise or services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the result of one of any number of operations of the machine is a matter of chance or uncertainty to the operator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a result of a given number of successive operations by the operator, the machine produces different results` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on any operation of the machine, it discharges or emits a slug or token` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(4.01) slot machine` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it is an automatic machine or slot machine`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "slot machine means any automatic machine or slot machine"
        IF `it dispenses as prizes only one or more free games on that machine` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than any automatic machine or slot machine that dispenses as prizes only one or more free games on that machine"
        IF `it is used or intended to be used for any purpose other than selling merchandise or services` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is used or intended to be used for the purpose of selling merchandise or services` AND (`the result of one of any number of operations of the machine is a matter of chance or uncertainty to the operator` OR `as a result of a given number of successive operations by the operator, the machine produces different results` OR `on any operation of the machine, it discharges or emits a slug or token`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "slot machine means any automatic machine or slot machine ... that (a) ... or (b) ... if (i) ... (ii) ... or (iii)"

-- src:4347 | (4.1) The use of a computer for the sale of a ticket, selection of a winner or the distribution of a prize in a raffle, including a 50/50 draw, is excluded from paragraph (4)(c) in so far as the raffle is authorized under paragraph (1)(b) and the proceeds are used for a charitable or religious object or purpose.
@ref s 207(4.1) (src:4347-4347)
GIVEN `it is the use of a computer for the sale of a ticket, selection of a winner or the distribution of a prize in a raffle, including a 50/50 draw` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the raffle is authorized under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeds are used for a charitable or religious object or purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(4.1) the use of a computer is excluded from paragraph (4)(c)` MEANS
    IF `it is the use of a computer for the sale of a ticket, selection of a winner or the distribution of a prize in a raffle, including a 50/50 draw` AND `the raffle is authorized under paragraph (1)(b)` AND `the proceeds are used for a charitable or religious object or purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is excluded from paragraph (4)(c) in so far as the raffle is authorized under paragraph (1)(b) and the proceeds are used for a charitable or religious object or purpose"

-- src:4349 | (5) For greater certainty, nothing in this section shall be construed as authorizing the making or recording of bets on horse-races through the agency of a pari-mutuel system other than in accordance with section 204.
@ref s 207(5) (src:4349-4349)
GIVEN `it is the making or recording of bets on horse-races through the agency of a pari-mutuel system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in accordance with section 204` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(5) section 207 authorizes the making or recording of the bets` MEANS
    IF `it is the making or recording of bets on horse-races through the agency of a pari-mutuel system` AND (NOT `it is in accordance with section 204`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section shall be construed as authorizing the making or recording of bets on horse-races through the agency of a pari-mutuel system other than in accordance with section 204"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what section 207 does not authorize; for bets in accordance with section 204 section 204 speaks

§ `Section 207.1 -- Lottery scheme on an international cruise ship`

-- src:4369 | (4) The definitions in this subsection apply in this section.
-- src:4370 | international cruise ship means a passenger ship that is suitable for continuous ocean voyages of at least forty-eight hours duration, but does not include such a ship that is used or fitted for the primary purpose of transporting cargo or vehicles. (navire de croisière internationale)
@ref s 207.1(4) (src:4369-4370)
GIVEN `it is a passenger ship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is suitable for continuous ocean voyages of at least forty-eight hours duration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used or fitted for the primary purpose of transporting cargo or vehicles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207.1(4) international cruise ship` MEANS
    IF `it is a passenger ship` AND `it is suitable for continuous ocean voyages of at least forty-eight hours duration` AND (NOT `it is used or fitted for the primary purpose of transporting cargo or vehicles`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "international cruise ship means a passenger ship that is suitable for continuous ocean voyages of at least forty-eight hours duration, but does not include such a ship that is used or fitted for the primary purpose of transporting cargo or vehicles"

-- src:4371 | lottery scheme means a game or any proposal, scheme, plan, means, device, contrivance or operation described in any of paragraphs 206(1)(a) to (g), whether or not it involves betting, pool selling or a pool system of betting. It does not include
-- src:4372 | (a) three-card monte, punch board or coin table; or
-- src:4373 | (b) bookmaking, pool selling or the making or recording of bets, including bets made through the agency of a pool or pari-mutuel system, on any race or fight, or on a single sporting event or athletic contest. (loterie)
@ref s 207.1(4) (lottery scheme) (src:4371-4373)
GIVEN `it is a game or any proposal, scheme, plan, means, device, contrivance or operation described in any of paragraphs 206(1)(a) to (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is three-card monte, punch board or coin table` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is bookmaking, pool selling or the making or recording of bets, including bets made through the agency of a pool or pari-mutuel system, on any race or fight, or on a single sporting event or athletic contest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207.1(4) lottery scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is three-card monte, punch board or coin table` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It does not include (a) three-card monte, punch board or coin table"
        IF `it is bookmaking, pool selling or the making or recording of bets, including bets made through the agency of a pool or pari-mutuel system, on any race or fight, or on a single sporting event or athletic contest` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It does not include ... (b) bookmaking, pool selling or the making or recording of bets"
        IF `it is a game or any proposal, scheme, plan, means, device, contrivance or operation described in any of paragraphs 206(1)(a) to (g)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "lottery scheme means a game or any proposal, scheme, plan, means, device, contrivance or operation described in any of paragraphs 206(1)(a) to (g)"

-- src:4351 | 207.1 (1) Despite any of the provisions of this Part relating to gaming and betting, it is lawful for the owner or operator of an international cruise ship, or their agent, to conduct, manage or operate and for any person to participate in a lottery scheme during a voyage on an international cruise ship when all of the following conditions are satisfied:
-- src:4352 | (a) all the people participating in the lottery scheme are located on the ship;
-- src:4353 | (b) the lottery scheme is not linked, by any means of communication, with any lottery scheme, betting, pool selling or pool system of betting located off the ship;
-- src:4354 | (c) the lottery scheme is not operated within five nautical miles of a Canadian port at which the ship calls or is scheduled to call; and
-- src:4355 | (d) the ship is registered
-- src:4356 | (i) in Canada and its entire voyage is scheduled to be outside Canada, or
-- src:4357 | (ii) anywhere, including Canada, and its voyage includes some scheduled voyaging within Canada and the voyage
-- src:4358 | (A) is of at least forty-eight hours duration and includes some voyaging in international waters and at least one non-Canadian port of call including the port at which the voyage begins or ends, and
-- src:4359 | (B) is not scheduled to disembark any passengers at a Canadian port who have embarked at another Canadian port, without calling on at least one non-Canadian port between the two Canadian ports.
@ref s 207.1(1) (src:4351-4359)
-- Fork F5: "the lottery scheme is not operated within five nautical miles of a Canadian port": a distance of exactly five nautical miles is within; the scheme complies only beyond five.
GIVEN `the lottery scheme is one conducted, managed or operated by the owner or operator of an international cruise ship, or their agent, or participated in by a person, during a voyage on the ship, by s 207.1(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `all the people participating in the lottery scheme are located on the ship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lottery scheme is linked, by any means of communication, with any lottery scheme, betting, pool selling or pool system of betting located off the ship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distance of the lottery scheme from a Canadian port at which the ship calls or is scheduled to call, in nautical miles` IS A NUMBER
      `the ship is registered in Canada and its entire voyage is scheduled to be outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship is registered anywhere, including Canada, and its voyage includes some scheduled voyaging within Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duration of the voyage, in hours` IS A NUMBER
      `the voyage includes some voyaging in international waters and at least one non-Canadian port of call including the port at which the voyage begins or ends` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voyage is scheduled to disembark passengers at a Canadian port who have embarked at another Canadian port, without calling on at least one non-Canadian port between the two Canadian ports` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207.1(1) makes it lawful to conduct, manage or operate, and to participate in, the lottery scheme during a voyage` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the lottery scheme is one conducted, managed or operated by the owner or operator of an international cruise ship, or their agent, or participated in by a person, during a voyage on the ship, by s 207.1(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of subsection (4) is itself not covered
        IF `the lottery scheme is one conducted, managed or operated by the owner or operator of an international cruise ship, or their agent, or participated in by a person, during a voyage on the ship, by s 207.1(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is lawful for the owner or operator of an international cruise ship, or their agent, to conduct, manage or operate ... a lottery scheme during a voyage on an international cruise ship"
        IF     `all the people participating in the lottery scheme are located on the ship`
           AND (NOT `the lottery scheme is linked, by any means of communication, with any lottery scheme, betting, pool selling or pool system of betting located off the ship`)
           AND `the distance of the lottery scheme from a Canadian port at which the ship calls or is scheduled to call, in nautical miles` GREATER THAN 5
           AND (   `the ship is registered in Canada and its entire voyage is scheduled to be outside Canada`
                OR (    `the ship is registered anywhere, including Canada, and its voyage includes some scheduled voyaging within Canada`
                    AND `the duration of the voyage, in hours` AT LEAST 48
                    AND `the voyage includes some voyaging in international waters and at least one non-Canadian port of call including the port at which the voyage begins or ends`
                    AND (NOT `the voyage is scheduled to disembark passengers at a Canadian port who have embarked at another Canadian port, without calling on at least one non-Canadian port between the two Canadian ports`)))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when all of the following conditions are satisfied" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4361 | (2) For greater certainty, paragraph 207(1)(h) and subsection 207(5) apply for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 207.1(2) (src:4361-4361)
GIVEN `the purpose is section 207.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207.1(2) paragraph 207(1)(h) and subsection 207(5) apply` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is section 207.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "paragraph 207(1)(h) and subsection 207(5) apply for the purposes of this section"

-- src:4363 | (3) Every one who, for the purpose of a lottery scheme, does anything that is not authorized by this section
-- src:4364 | (a) in the case of the conduct, management or operation of the lottery scheme,
-- src:4365 | (i) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years, or
-- src:4366 | (ii) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction; and
-- src:4367 | (b) in the case of participating in the lottery scheme, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 207.1(3) (src:4363-4367)
DECLARE `s 207.1(3) role` IS ONE OF
    `s 207.1(3)(a) the person conducts, manages or operates the lottery scheme`
    `s 207.1(3)(b) the person participates in the lottery scheme`

@ref s 207.1(3) (src:4363-4367)
GIVEN `the thing is done for the purpose of a lottery scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is authorized by section 207.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207.1(3) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the thing is done for the purpose of a lottery scheme` AND (NOT `it is authorized by section 207.1`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who, for the purpose of a lottery scheme, does anything that is not authorized by this section" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 207.1(3) (src:4363-4367)
GIVEN role IS A `s 207.1(3) role`
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 207.1(3) the class of the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER role
    WHEN `s 207.1(3)(a) the person conducts, manages or operates the lottery scheme` THEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
    WHEN `s 207.1(3)(b) the person participates in the lottery scheme` THEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 207.1(3)(a)(i) (src:4365-4365)
`s 207.1(3)(a)(i) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 207.1(3) (src:4363-4367)
GIVEN role IS A `s 207.1(3) role`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 207.1(3) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER role
    WHEN `s 207.1(3)(a) the person conducts, manages or operates the lottery scheme` THEN LIST `s 207.1(3)(a)(i) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
    WHEN `s 207.1(3)(b) the person participates in the lottery scheme` THEN LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 209 -- Cheating at play`

-- src:4376 | 209 Every person who, with intent to defraud any person, cheats while playing a game or in holding the stakes for a game or in betting is guilty of
-- src:4377 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:4378 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 209 (src:4376-4378)
GIVEN `the person cheats while playing a game, or in holding the stakes for a game, or in betting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so with intent to defraud any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209 the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person cheats while playing a game, or in holding the stakes for a game, or in betting` AND `the person does so with intent to defraud any person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who, with intent to defraud any person, cheats while playing a game or in holding the stakes for a game or in betting is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 209 (src:4376-4378)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 209 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 209(a) (src:4377-4377)
`s 209(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 209 (src:4376-4378)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 209 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 209(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 213 -- Offences in relation to offering, providing or obtaining sexual services for consideration`

-- src:4392 | (2) In this section, public place includes any place to which the public have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied, and any motor vehicle located in a public place or in any place open to public view.
@ref s 213(2) (src:4392-4392)
GIVEN `the public have access to it as of right or by invitation, express or implied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a motor vehicle located in a public place or in any place open to public view` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(2) public place` MEANS
    IF `the public have access to it as of right or by invitation, express or implied` OR `it is a motor vehicle located in a public place or in any place open to public view`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "public place includes any place to which the public have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied, and any motor vehicle located in a public place or in any place open to public view"

-- src:4385 | 213 (1) Everyone is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, in a public place or in any place open to public view, for the purpose of offering, providing or obtaining sexual services for consideration,
-- src:4386 | (a) stops or attempts to stop any motor vehicle; or
-- src:4387 | (b) impedes the free flow of pedestrian or vehicular traffic or ingress to or egress from premises adjacent to that place.
@ref s 213(1) (src:4385-4387)
GIVEN `the person is in a public place or in any place open to public view, by s 213(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of offering, providing or obtaining sexual services for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person stops or attempts to stop a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person impedes the free flow of pedestrian or vehicular traffic or ingress to or egress from premises adjacent to that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(1) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF     `the person is in a public place or in any place open to public view, by s 213(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `it is for the purpose of offering, providing or obtaining sexual services for consideration`
       AND (`the person stops or attempts to stop a motor vehicle` OR `the person impedes the free flow of pedestrian or vehicular traffic or ingress to or egress from premises adjacent to that place`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, in a public place or in any place open to public view, for the purpose of offering, providing or obtaining sexual services for consideration, (a) stops or attempts to stop any motor vehicle; or (b) impedes" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 213(1) (src:4385-4387)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 213(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 213(1) (src:4385-4387)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 213(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4390 | (1.1) Everyone is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who communicates with any person — for the purpose of offering or providing sexual services for consideration — in a public place, or in any place open to public view, that is or is next to a school ground, playground or daycare centre.
@ref s 213(1.1) (src:4390-4390)
GIVEN `the person communicates with any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of offering or providing sexual services for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a public place, or in any place open to public view, by s 213(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that place is or is next to a school ground, playground or daycare centre` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(1.1) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF     `the person communicates with any person`
       AND `it is for the purpose of offering or providing sexual services for consideration`
       AND `it is in a public place, or in any place open to public view, by s 213(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `that place is or is next to a school ground, playground or daycare centre`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who communicates with any person — for the purpose of offering or providing sexual services for consideration — in a public place, or in any place open to public view, that is or is next to a school ground, playground or daycare centre" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 213(1.1) (src:4390-4390)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 213(1.1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 213(1.1) (src:4390-4390)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 213(1.1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
